  "finalMessage": "Porto Notes is built and shipping. `pnpm build` → `dist/` (3 static files), `pnpm smoke` → OK, `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n\n## What's there\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `index.html` | Static shell: labelled form, search, `#results-line`, `#feed` |\n| `src/main.ts` | State, rendering, events, fragment sync |\n| `src/richtext.ts` | Allowlist rich-text renderer + URL checks |\n| `src/storage.ts` | localStorage load/save, fixtures seeding |\n| `src/fragment.ts` | `#q=…&note=…` parse/serialise |\n| `src/types.ts`, `src/style.css`, `src/fixtures.json` | Types, styles, seed data |\n\nElement contract implemented exactly as specified: `#note-form` with `#title`/`#body`/`#avatar` + submit, `#search`, `p#results-line` showing `results for \"<query>\"`, `#feed` of `article.note[data-note-id]` with `.note-title`/`.note-body`/`img.note-avatar`, `aria-current=\"true\"` on the selected note, and fragment sync in `q`-then-`note` order via `replaceState` (no history spam while typing, no loop with the `hashchange` handler that adopts back/forward and hand-edited URLs).\n\n## Two judgement calls worth knowing\n\n**Rich text is a tokenizer, not a filter.** `renderRichText` walks the input, escapes every text run, and re-emits only `<b> <strong> <i> <em> <a href> <br>`. Anything else — `<script>`, `<img onerror>`, an `onclick` on an allowed tag — is escaped and displayed literally, so no markup reaches the DOM that the renderer didn't construct. Hrefs are entity-decoded and control-stripped before the scheme check, since `&#106;avascript:` and `java\\tscript:` both parse as `javascript:`. Unclosed tags are auto-closed so one note's stray `<b>` can't bold the rest of the feed. Titles render inside their `<button>`, so anchors there degrade to their text rather than nesting invalidly.\n\n**A selected note that the query hides stays selected but isn't rendered** — search filters, and the selection lives on in state and the fragment, reappearing when the query clears. Flagging this because the request's own example, `#q=port&note=3`, is inconsistent with the fixtures: note 3 (\"Francesinha ranking\") doesn't contain \"port\", so under strict filtering that exact URL restores the query but shows no `aria-current` anywhere. I read the example as illustrating fragment *format* — the alternative, pinning selected notes outside their search results, would contradict \"a search box that filters notes\" and would break result counts. If the shared suite asserts `aria-current` on that literal URL, this is the line to revisit.\n\nI verified with a temporary 43-assertion Playwright harness (since deleted) covering the element contract, newest-first order, formatting, case-insensitive search, selection, deep-link restore, `hashchange`, id sequencing, persistence across reload, and 11 injection payloads across title/body/avatar — no script execution, no `on*` attributes or `javascript:` URLs in the feed, and none after reload from storage. It also caught two things I then fixed: avatars no longer accept relative URLs (a typo'd avatar was firing requests back at the app), and a broken avatar image removes itself rather than leaving an artifact.",
